# Hand-written, not autogenerated (see c240c2157e8a for the same practice):
# these three columns were declared without DateTime(timezone=True), unlike
# every other timestamp column in the schema (TimestampMixin,
# Verification.last_run_at, Target.ownership_verified_at, ...). It went
# unnoticed because a single-row UPDATE tolerates the mismatch; a batched
# UPDATE across multiple Persona rows in one flush does not (asyncpg:
# "can't subtract offset-naive and offset-aware datetimes") — found while
# wiring AUTH_ESTABLISHING for more than one persona at once (M2 slice 1).
# `USING` casts are safe no-op reinterpretations here: every existing value
# was always produced by `datetime.now(UTC)`, so treating the stored
# instant as UTC is exactly correct, not a guess.


